WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.553 --> 00:00:04.490
1990.

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:06.100
The famous Bank of China building

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.540
became the newest addition
to the Hong Kong skyline

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:12.200
with its sharp, pointed edges.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.170
Soon after the building was opened,

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:17.460
the bank next door reported huge losses

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:20.170
and two other businesses
filed for bankruptcy.

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:23.920
Those businesses
specifically blame the design

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:27.570
of the Bank of China building
for causing this catastrophe.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:28.470
Why?

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.940
Because with those sharp edges,

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:35.141
that building shirks the
principles of feng shui,

00:00:35.141 --> 00:00:39.200
supposedly cutting through
the skyline's good fortune.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:42.100
It may seem like superstition,

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.070
but architects from around the world

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:47.570
have made major design
decisions based on feng shui,

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:49.440
decisions that we can see

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:52.180
and that may even affect our lives.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:53.900
So, what is feng shui?

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:57.030
It's all about creating
harmony by finding ways

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:00.360
to connect manmade things with nature

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.530
through design using the
five natural elements:

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:04.363
metal,

00:01:05.347 --> 00:01:07.127
water,

00:01:07.127 --> 00:01:08.810
wood,

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:09.643
fire,

00:01:10.626 --> 00:01:11.459
and earth.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:18.530
The best way to understand
it is to start small,

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:20.130
with a living room.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:22.920
And each one promotes something different.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:25.530
Water can represent living flexibly,

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:28.670
and you can include it in your
home using the color black

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:31.480
or by introducing a wavy pattern.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:35.730
Metal is represented by
objects made of, well, metal,

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:37.260
as well as the color white.

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:40.730
You'd add fire elements if
you want to ignite passion.

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:42.290
Triangular shapes and the color red

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:44.360
help to bring in a little heat.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:47.340
The wood element can
encourage personal growth,

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.940
and you can incorporate that
with the color green in plants.

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:54.190
Finally, earth elements provide stability,

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:56.760
and you can incorporate
it by adding heavy objects

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.210
or something like a square rug.

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:01.740
It's solid but can be refined.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:04.610
Good for creating stronger focus

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:07.720
and disrupting unharmonious forces.

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:10.120
It may seem unlikely that these practices

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:13.010
can bring about such major life results,

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:15.900
but there's a reason some of
the world's most successful

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:19.980
and impressive architects
integrate them into their designs.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:22.670
Put simply, they share the same purpose:

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:24.630
to figure out the needs of a person

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:27.970
and find ways to make
the space functional.

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:32.310
This can be done by using
colors, shapes, textures,

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:36.510
and even through the arrangement
of things like furniture.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:47.040
To see how architects use feng shui,

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:48.965
let's start in New York City

00:02:48.965 --> 00:02:50.890
at the famous Columbus Circle,

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:53.340
one of the first major locations

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:56.170
to use feng shui in the United States.

00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:57.960
It's right next to Central Park,

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:01.110
and the central feature
is this roundabout.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:04.910
Roundabouts represent a
huge problem in feng shui.

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:06.560
They represent the water element,

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:09.990
but in a more volatile way: whirlpools.

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:13.010
There's an endless rotation
of people, vehicles,

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:16.240
and energy constantly flowing
through the traffic circle.

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:19.910
Like water, without something
to interrupt the flow,

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:21.870
a whirlpool begins to form.

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:25.630
Feng shui experts say this
can cause catastrophe,

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:29.370
as wealth could potentially get
sucked into the hectic flow.

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:31.950
One of those businesses
concerned about this

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:34.610
is the Trump International Hotel.

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:38.140
Enter feng shui master and
Trump consultant in the '90s

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:41.120
Pun-Yin and her father, Tin-Sun.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:45.600
She suggested adding the now
famous Columbus Circle globe,

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:48.870
which literally disrupts
the flow of energy

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:51.130
as people stop and gather around.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:54.210
Its purpose is to stop the roundabout

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:57.800
from sucking in all the potential
wealth and opportunities.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:00.190
For example, people who may have otherwise

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:03.680
just kept walking are
stopped in their tracks,

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.833
potentially bringing in more business

00:04:05.833 --> 00:04:08.213
and, therefore, more wealth.

00:04:12.227 --> 00:04:15.913
The globe was installed
in 1996 by Donald Trump

00:04:15.913 --> 00:04:19.185
at the suggestion of the
two feng shui masters.

00:04:19.185 --> 00:04:21.860
The move signaled to the
architecture community

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:24.960
that there was a new
market emerging in the US

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:27.760
for feng shui in architectural design.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:30.990
After this, the number
of feng shui businesses

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:35.773
in New York state shot up from two to 65.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:39.340
Feng shui is used by
architects in different places

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:42.260
around the world for different reasons.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:45.050
But whether the architect
has a casual interest in it,

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:47.030
is culturally connected to it,

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:50.380
or simply knows it helps sell
newly developed buildings,

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:53.350
it's being used everywhere.

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:57.330
Next, let's take a trip
to Sydney, Australia,

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.470
home to the Sydney Opera House,

00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:02.830
a feng shui triumph by
combining two elements

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:06.310
that seem at opposition
but actually work together:

00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:08.390
fire and water.

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:12.040
It was designed by architect Jørn Utzon,

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:16.570
who wanted to create a
space that uplifts the arts.

00:05:16.570 --> 00:05:18.150
According to Steven Post,

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:20.280
a feng shui practitioner and teacher,

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:22.130
the sail-like curves of the structure,

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:23.893
which is literally built on water,

00:05:23.893 --> 00:05:26.193
represent that element and combine

00:05:26.193 --> 00:05:27.770
with the triangular shapes,

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:29.920
which represent fire in feng shui,

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:31.961
that prop up those curves.

00:05:31.961 --> 00:05:35.820
This combination can create
a productive balance,

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:37.400
using the passion of the arts

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:40.210
to foster flexibility in its audiences

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:41.540
and the largest city.

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:44.810
That makes sense because
the Sydney Opera House

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:47.093
is all about promoting
the performing arts.

00:05:47.949 --> 00:05:49.760
Hopping over to Europe,

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:53.810
let's look to the romance
capitol of the world, Paris,

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:56.910
which is home to the most
famous collection of art

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:59.143
in the Western world, the Louvre.

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:03.340
It was designed by I. M.
Pei, the same architect

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:06.420
who designed the "disastrous"
Bank of China building

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:10.510
in Hong Kong, but this
one is a feng shui marvel.

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:14.260
The Louvre includes classic
European architecture

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:17.260
coupled with more modern
glass pyramids in the center.

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:19.180
Pyramidal structures are regarded

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:22.427
as a classic fire structure in feng shui,

00:06:22.427 --> 00:06:25.450
and its base is flat and square,

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:28.120
representing the element of earth.

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.310
The combination of these two elements

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:33.070
encourages passion through
the element of fire

00:06:33.070 --> 00:06:36.250
to fuel the need for art
to continuously evolve,

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:39.140
while the earth element
helps ground the place

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:42.260
and teaches us to respect
the invaluable treasures

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:45.670
of classical art that are
already in the museum.

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:48.423
But not all buildings can be so lucky.

00:06:49.691 --> 00:06:51.030
The Bank of China building

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:53.130
had one of its sharp edges

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:56.330
pointed directly at the HSBC building,

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:58.250
the neighboring bank that reported losses

00:06:58.250 --> 00:06:59.620
as a result of this.

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:04.440
So HSBC responded with feng
shui adjustments of their own

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:06.430
by installing canon-like structures

00:07:06.430 --> 00:07:08.100
on the top of their building,

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:12.030
a feng shui tradition that
deflects negative energy.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:15.840
But experts say there are
a few relatively easy fixes

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:18.390
that could put the
building back in harmony.

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:20.340
Steven Post says changing

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:23.720
the crisscrossing metal
components from white to green

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:25.290
would promote wood energy

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:27.730
and making the antenna at the top red

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:29.730
would promote fire energy.

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:32.720
Making these changes would
shift the sharp nature

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:36.030
of the building into a
naturally harmonious one,

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:40.280
where wood is fueling the
fire, leading to success.

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:43.250
As architects and interior
designers continue

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:46.330
to include the practice of
feng shui into their work,

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:49.470
you can expect to see more
buildings and landmarks

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:53.980
with the aim of creating a
healthy, harmonious city life.

00:07:53.980 --> 00:07:55.860
Maybe one day, they'll be able

00:07:55.860 --> 00:07:59.440
to even remedy the growing
feeling of fleeing big cities

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:01.320
for wide-open spaces.

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:03.200
So, the next time you're out and about

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:06.040
in your own neighborhoods,
take a look around.

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:08.680
There could be feng shui elements at work

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:10.080
and you didn't even know it.

